An object that fills the rest of its pool exactly does not fit,
where the room OP_POOL_INFO tells says it does.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: an allocation's room differs from the pool's
Witness: fuzz pool-info-fills

diff --git a/kernel/pool.c b/kernel/pool.c
--- a/kernel/pool.c
+++ b/kernel/pool.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ bool pool_destroy(struct pool *pool, bool preempt)
 
 bool pool_fits(const struct pool *pool, size_t size)
 {
-    return obj_align((uint32_t)size) <= pool->size - pool->used;
+    return obj_align((uint32_t)size) < pool->size - pool->used;
 }
 
 void *pool_alloc(struct pool *pool, uint8_t type, size_t size)
